---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Backend and infrastructure engineer. Self-hosts everything on one VPS."
>
  <section class="pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-[length:var(--text-title)]">About</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-10">
      <!-- TODO(pawan): this is scaffolding built from what is verifiable in your
           repos. Replace it with your own words before this goes live. -->
      <p>
        I work on backend and infrastructure — mostly Go, with enough React to
        build the interfaces on top of it. I prefer systems that are boring to
        operate: one binary, one process, no runtime dependencies to drift.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everything I run lives on a VPS I administer myself, deployed through a
        self-hosted PaaS rather than a managed platform. That is partly
        stubbornness and partly the fastest way I know to actually learn how the
        pieces fit together.
      </p>

      <h3>How this site is built</h3>

      <p>
        The site is a static build compiled into a Go binary and shipped in a
        container with nothing else in it. The origin serves pre-compressed
        bytes, picks the encoding by measured size rather than by reputation, and
        drains cleanly on shutdown so deploys drop nothing. There is no
        JavaScript on the page you are reading.
      </p>

      <p>
        The <a href="/perf/">measurements page</a> publishes what visitors
        actually experience, rather than a Lighthouse screenshot taken on a good
        day.
      </p>

